<p>These ranges represent 17-year-olds with normal athletic activity but no dedicated speed training. Varsity athletes who play speed-dependent sports typically run 0.3 to 0.5 seconds faster than the population average.</p>
<p>Seventeen is junior year — the single most important recruiting evaluation year in high school football. The bulk of D1 scholarship offers are made between October of junior year and April of senior year. <strong>What you run at 17 is what coaches are making decisions from.</strong></p>

